{"name":"Placebo Pink","hex":"#fcebfa","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"placebo","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A dummy medicine containing no active ingredients; an inert treatment. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","The vespers sung in the office for the dead."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/placebo"},{"term":"pink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A color reminiscent of pinks, the flowers.","Magenta, the colour evoked by red and blue light when combined."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a colour between red and white; pale red.","Of a fox-hunter's jacket: scarlet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pink"}],"entries":[{"title":"Placebo","blocks":[{"text":"A placebo is a medicine or treatment intended to appear genuine to its recipient, but which has no pharmaceutical effect. Common placebos include inert tablets, inert injections, sham surgery, and other procedures."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Cebocap.jpg/330px-Cebocap.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Placebo","wikidata":"Q269829"},{"title":"Pink","blocks":[{"text":"Pink is a pale tint of red or rose, the color of the pink flower. It was first used as a color name in the late 17th century. A combination of pink and white is associated with innocence, whereas a combination of pink and black links to eroticism and seduction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg/330px-Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pink","wikidata":"Q429220"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/%22Miracle_Cure%21%22_Health_Fraud_Scams_%288528312890%29.jpg/500px-%22Miracle_Cure%21%22_Health_Fraud_Scams_%288528312890%29.jpg?utm_sourc